render.yaml at the Excalidraw cut-over: the prepared change, NOT applied
=========================================================================

Prepared 2026-09-30 on engine/w4-prep against render.yaml as it is on main and engine/excalidraw (the two
are identical). It is kept here, and not in render.yaml, on purpose: staging's Blueprint has synced
render.yaml on pushes to main and deployed the services whose environment changed, so editing render.yaml
early could switch staging before the cut-over, in an order no one controls.

When and how (docs/EXCALIDRAW-CUTOVER.md):
- The /excalidraw-assets/* rewrite is tried alone on the static site first, by hand (step P6), because
  Render's answer to it is UNVERIFIED.
- At the cut-over every value is set by hand, one service at a time, in the runbook's order: sync's
  DRAFTROOM_ENGINE and DRAFTROOM_BOOT_MAINTENANCE=1 (C8), then the web's CSP header and VITE_LOBBY_ENGINE
  (C13). DRAFTROOM_BOOT_MAINTENANCE is deleted again once maintenance is off (C16).
- Only after that, with the Blueprint on Manual Sync (P8), this patch is committed (C19):
      git apply docs/research/excalidraw/render.cutover.yaml.patch
  with the CSP line corrected to the Clerk origins the rehearsal records (P5, R8). The Blueprint's sync
  preview must then show nothing to apply.

What it changes:
1. web routes: a rewrite of /excalidraw-assets/* to a path that does not exist, BEFORE the SPA fallback,
   so a missing font file is a 404 and never index.html (plan §2.12; spike A12 finding 3).
2. web headers: the Content-Security-Policy of plan §2.12 / spike A12 (staging form): no 'unsafe-eval', no
   inline-script hash (index.html's theme script moves to a file, wave 4), font-src 'self' (the font
   fallback is same-origin through the host-rewrite plugin), the sync origin for the board socket, and
   Clerk's origins (the frontend-API host decoded from staging's public publishable key on 2026-09-30:
   splendid-flamingo-3744.clerk.accounts.dev, a development instance; img.clerk.com and
   clerk-telemetry.com from @clerk/shared's code; challenges.cloudflare.com from Clerk's documentation:
   all UNVERIFIED until a real sign-in with the header enforced, at the rehearsal).
3. web env: VITE_LOBBY_ENGINE=excalidraw added; VITE_TLDRAW_LICENSE_KEY removed from the file. Its value
   stays on the service until drop-legacy (day 7), so that a rollback can still rebuild R0's web.
4. sync env: DRAFTROOM_ENGINE=excalidraw; DRAFTROOM_BOOT_MAINTENANCE declared `sync: false`, so a Blueprint
   sync never sets it (a value of "1" left in place would start every later deploy and restart with every
   board closed). The flag is not implemented yet (plan open item 11; runbook §1 G1).
5. The sync service's comment no longer says "tldraw rooms".

Checked 2026-09-30: `git apply --check` against render.yaml at engine/excalidraw 1a85d5c; the patched file
parses as YAML (yaml 2) with the same three services, the routes in this order (/api/*, /files/*,
/excalidraw-assets/*, /*) and the CSP value on one line; and both the current and the patched file
validate against Render's published schema (https://render.com/schema/render.yaml.json, fetched that
day, ajv 8). The schema cannot tell whether Render answers the rewrite with a 404 (step P6).

